%% Ask my course (requirement 0006) — the request path, and where 0010 bounds it.
%% Derived from ADR 0013 (managed hybrid index), ADR 0014 (bounded loop, consent before widening),
%% ADR 0016 (scope is an allow-list), ADR 0008 (event in the same write), spec 0010, CLAUDE.md.
%% Changed 2026-09-29. ADR 0001 (scope query) and ADR 0007 (one request) are superseded.
%% NOT YET DECIDED: the citation check. ADR 0002 validated a cited session against the scope the
%% product SENT; retrieval now chooses it, so that record must be superseded and its successor is
%% not written. The check drawn below is CLAUDE.md's re-founded five-step invariant, which binds
%% requirement 0006 and awaits an ADR. Do not build from this box.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor L as Learner
  participant W as apps/web
  participant A as apps/api
  participant F as Firestore
  participant R as RAG Engine — this learner's corpus
  participant G as Gemini (Vertex AI)

  L->>W: a question, and optionally the sessions to ask it against
  W->>A: question + sessionIds — Bearer ID token
  A->>F: the learner's corpus, and the material they hold now
  F-->>A: corpus  ·  allow-list of ragFile ids  ·  what is still reading
  Note over A: readableSet() — the one place that answers<br/>"what may this request read?" (spec 0010)
  alt material for these sessions is still being read
    A-->>W: say so and name it — never a thinner answer that looks complete (0010, AIT-82)
  end
  rect rgb(238,246,255)
    Note over A,R: PHASE ONE — inside the scope the learner chose<br/>bound: 3 steps · 12,000 retrieved tokens · 15 s, whichever binds first (ADR 0014)
    loop until grounded, or the bound binds
      A->>R: retrieve — allow-list narrowed to the named sessions<br/>dense + sparse, rank-fused (ADR 0013, ADR 0016)
      R-->>A: contexts { sourceUri, text, score }
      A->>A: assert every context maps to the allow-list<br/>a foreign context is an IsolationFault — withheld and reported, never retried
    end
  end
  alt phase one found nothing sufficient
    A-->>W: the chosen sessions do not cover this  ·  may I look wider?
    W-->>L: the offer  ·  nothing outside the scope has been read yet
    L->>W: yes
    W->>A: the same question, with consent for this question only
    rect rgb(255,247,235)
      Note over A,R: PHASE TWO — the learner's whole corpus, never beyond it<br/>same bound again · consent is never remembered (Intent 0006 NOT NOW)
      A->>R: retrieve — the full allow-list
      R-->>A: contexts
    end
  end
  A->>A: label every chunk "Document 3 = Session 5 · Thermodynamics · lecture slides"<br/>the model never sees a session id, so it cannot invent one
  A->>G: one structured request  ·  response schema with citations[] by label
  G-->>A: { answer, cited: [labels], covered }
  rect rgb(245,245,245)
    Note over A: CITATION CHECK — awaiting ADR 0002's successor.<br/>Drop any label outside the set sent · withhold a grounded answer that cites nothing verifiable
  end
  alt nothing the learner owns covers it
    A-->>W: say so plainly and name what appears missing — never a guess from general knowledge
  else answered
    A->>F: the event, in the same write — ADR 0008<br/>{ learner, requirement: 0006, attributes: { steps, phase, termination, cost } }
    A-->>W: answer + citations, naming any session outside the original scope
    W-->>L: the answer names its session  ·  one click reaches the source material itself
  end
